 linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2y+3z+x=-1 \\\\ 4z+y=1 \\\\ 5x+6y-3=-3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186096368 "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0.5x+3y+4=0 \\\\ 4x=-20y-20\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186096369 "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}1.4x+2.8y=1.4 \\\\ 0.02x+0.01y=0.05\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186096388 "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=-4 \\\\ x-\\frac{y}{6}=\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186096389 "Find the solution to the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5a+\\frac{3b}{2}=2 \\\\ \\frac{4a}{3}+2b=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186096394 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-x-5y=-1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}x+3y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the system of equations given above."] [#edb/ref 17592186096395 "Find the solution to the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2}x+2y=3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{6}x-\\frac{2}{3}y=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186096546 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y=2 \\\\ x-4z=6 \\\\ -3x+6y=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system."] [#edb/ref 17592186096547 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-6y+2z=8 \\\\ -6x+18y-6z=-24 \\\\ 4x-12y+4z=16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form."] [#edb/ref 17592186096924 "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y-z=10 \\\\  & y+5z=15 \\\\  & -z=5\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186097174 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+z=2 \\\\  & x+