 $ and $\\mu $ satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}⟨1,\\,2y,\\,1⟩=\\lambda ⟨0,\\,\\bbox[2pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AA}},\\,2z⟩+\\mu ⟨1,\\,\\bbox[2pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AA}},\\,2z⟩ \\\\ 3{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=2 \\\\ x+{z}^{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing expressions?"] [#edb/ref 17592186175768 "Suppose that $f(x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{x-1}, & x\\ne 1 \\\\ \\,\\,1, & x=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIs the extreme value theorem applicable to $f(x)$ on the intervals $[-1,2]$ and $[-1,0]?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186175834 "The second-order differential equation \n\n$$\ny''  - 7t y' + e^{t}y= -t\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}=f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $x_1(t) = y(t)$ and $x_2(t) = y'(t).$ Find the function $f(t).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186175847 "Consider the third-order differential equation\n\n$$\ny''' + t y' - 8 y = 1 - t^2,\n$$\n\nwhere $y = y(t).$ If\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y={x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}={x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {y}^{″}={x}_{3}(t),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthen the given differential equation can be rewritten as the matrix equation $\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t) + \\mathbf f(t),$ where\n![](images/2b/2b3ba6edd838ee516ad902008726afbca516ab15892aad0f236c5a2270261985.png)\nDetermine the matrices $A$ and $\\mathbf{f}(t).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186176222 "The third-order differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}-\\sqrt{t}\\,{y}^{″}-y={t}^{2}\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}=f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{′}(t)$ and ${x}_{3}(t)={y}^{″}(t).$ Find the function $f(t).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186176258 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{3}{x}^{3}y, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the marginal PDF ${f}_{Y}(y).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186176261 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}), & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(0.2<X<1).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186176262 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}4xy, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe marginal CDF ${F}_{X}(x)$ of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n{F}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ g(x), & 0\\le x\\le 1 \\\\ 1 & x>1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat is the function $g(x)?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186176276 "![](images/c6/c64cfa701997c2b9e5e54f7eb77afb9927b878065af9c32fed86f09f140a4ec4.png)\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables with the joint probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y, & (x,y)\\in D, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $F(x,y)$ is the joint CDF of $X$ and $Y,$ find $F(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{5}).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186176373 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables with the joint probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{2}{y}^{2}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 3, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the corresponding joint CDF when $x>1,\\,y>3.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186176374 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables with the joint probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{2}{y}^{2}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 3, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the corresponding joint CDF when $x<0,\\,1<y<3.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186176376 "A random va