ble $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{50}x,\\, & 0\\le x\\le 10, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186193390 "Compute $P(X\\ge 5)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}8{e}^{-8x},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & x<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186193391 "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}k{e}^{-3x},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186193392 "Compute $P(X>8)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}},\\, & x\\ge 3, \\\\ 0,\\, & x<3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186198228 "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the ellipsoid $\\dfrac{x^2}{24} + \\dfrac{y^2}{24} +\\dfrac{z^2}{6} = 1$ and the line \n$\\{\\begin{aligned}x=4t \\\\ y=8t, \\\\ z=2t\\end{aligned}$ \nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186198993 "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the ellipsoid $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}=1$ and the line \n${\\begin{aligned}x=t \\\\ y=2t, \\\\ z=t\\end{aligned}$ where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186198998 "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the ellipsoid $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{6}=1$ and the line \n$\\{\\begin{aligned}x=t \\\\ y=1-t, \\\\ z=t+2\\end{aligned}$ where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186221148 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-4{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs above, where $t\\in\\mathbb R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The function ![](images/74/74e10d18890ebd27b2339e13ac2bbc9e0821c1dfea752478a90877d0a0059ff6.png) is a solution of the system.\n\n- The function ![](images/f0/f0