, & x<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186262577 "Compute $P(X>1)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}0.1{e}^{-0.1x},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & x<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186262578 "Compute $P(X>4)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}},\\, & x\\ge 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186262579 "Compute $P(X>2)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{(1+x)^{2}},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186262580 "Compute $P(X\\ge 2)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{2-2x},\\, & x\\ge 1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186262682 "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2+4t \\\\ y=\\frac{3}{4}-2t \\\\ z=3+t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat would be the vector equation of the line?"] [#edb/ref 17592186262683 "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-3 \\\\ y=5t \\\\ z=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat would be the vector equation of the line?"] [#edb/ref 17592186262684 "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=11 \\\\ y=3+7t \\\\ z=-5t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat would be the vector equation of the line?"] [#edb/ref 17592186262694 "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=\\frac{1}{3}t-2 \\\\ y=5-4t \\\\ z=2t+\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line."] [#edb/ref 17592186262767 "Consider the straight line with the parametric equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1-2t \\\\ y=5-t \\\\ z=-7+t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nf