owing could be the definition of the rectangular domain $R?$\n\n- $R=[0,1]\\times [-1,1]$\n- $R=[0,2]\\times [-1,1]$\n- $R=[0,2]\\times [0,1]$\n\nSelect all that apply."] [#edb/ref 17592186348410 "![](images/50/506a298041a875549ec60c5cf99ebdbeb5ca4b5717037083fa6ca196fce27279.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If $R=[-2,2]\\times [0,3],$ and\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\frac{2x+y}{y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of $f(x,y)?$\n\nI. $\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+y}{y}, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\notin D\\end{aligned}$\n\nII. $\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & (x,y)\\in R \\\\ \\frac{2x+y}{y}, & (x,y)\\in D∖R\\end{aligned}$\n\nIII. $\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+y}{y}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}$\n\nSelect all that apply."] [#edb/ref 17592186348412 "![](images/d9/d92fdb93f7564e1c205ab8603945eb6704c03db92c46130810e2b7cbce9a0e20.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+xy & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${∬}_{R}({x}^{2}+xy)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[0,2]\\times [-1,1]$\n- ${∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+xy)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[0,2]\\times [-2,2]$\n- ${∬}_{R}({x}^{2}+xy)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[0,3]\\times [-2,2]$\n\nSelect all that apply."] [#edb/ref 17592186348413 "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed between the curve $y={x}^{2}-4$ and the $x$-axis. If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}3x-y, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${∬}_{D}(3x-y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-3,2]\\times [-4,1]$\n- **II.** ${∬}_{R}(3x-y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-3,3]\\times [-4,4]$\n- **III.** ${∬}_{D}(3x-y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [-4,0]$"] [#edb/ref 17592186351256 "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186351257 "Given the vector $x$ and the system of  linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186351279 "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$, where\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2},\\, & \\text{if}\\,1<x<9,\\,-1<y<1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{xy}},\\, & \\text{if}\\,1<x<9,\\,1<y<4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand  $R$ is the domain of $f.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186351525 "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}-20 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+12{x}_{2}-12{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186354522 "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186354528 "![](images/47/4772b690cb85fcb4dffd27ac4ba56344307ca106e927b9945144370b266d2be9.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}y, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,{∬}_{D}{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of the rectangular domain $R?$\n\n- $R=[0,2]\\times [-1,1]$\n- $R=[-1,0]\\times [0,1]$\n- $R=[-1,2]\\times [-2,2]$\n\nSelect all that apply."] [#edb/ref 17592186354529 "![](images/53/534f6ef0206bd4281320968c8a60b88f7f237e48c31e3d10c1080ddb69b9f56f.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-{y}^{3}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,{∬}_{D}({x}^{2}-{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of the rectangular domain $R?$\n\nI. $R=[-1,2]\\times [0,1]$\n\nII. $R=[-1,2]\\times [-2,2]$\n\nIII. $R=[-2,2]\\times [0,1]$\n\nSelect all that apply."] [#edb/ref 17592186354530 "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed by the curve $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1.$ If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x-y}, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${∬}_{D}{e}^{x-y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [-3,3]$\n\n- **II.** ${∬}_{R}{e}^{x-y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [-3,3]$\n\n- **III.** ${∬}_{D}{e}^{x-y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-3,3]\\times [-2,2]$"] [#edb/ref 17592186354532 "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed by the curves $y={x}^{2}-1$ and $y=|x|.$ If $R=[-2,2]\\times [-1,2],$ and\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of $f(x,y)?$\n\nI. $\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+1}, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\notin D\\end{aligned}$\n\nII. $\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+1}, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}$\n\nIII. $\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+1}, & (x,y)\\in R \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\notin R\\end{aligned}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked."] [#edb/ref 17592186354533 "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed by the curves $y=-|x|+2$ and $y=|x|.$ If $R=[-1,1]\\times [0,2],$ and\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}({x}^{5}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of $f(x,y)?$\n\nI. $\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{5}-{y}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\notin D\\end{aligned}$\n\nII. $\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{5}-{y}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}$\n\nIII. $\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{5}-{y}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in R \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\notin R\\end{aligned}$\n\nSelect all that apply."] [#edb/ref 17592186354536 "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k}{{x}^{2}},\\, & 2<x\\le 10, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186354555 "Compute $P(X>6)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{-3x},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & x<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186354557 "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k}{{x}^{3}},\\, & 3<x<6, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186354558 "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}k{e}^{-5x},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186354559 "Solve for $k$ given that the following function is a probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}k{e}^{6x},\\, & x\\le 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186354631 "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y=1 \\\\ x-8y=-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186357405 "Find $L{f(t)}$ for the piecewise function defined by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & t<1 \\\\ -7,\\, & 1\\le t\\le 3 \\\\ 0,\\, & t>3.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186357670 "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)=4{x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n\\boxed{}\\,{y}_{1}^{2}-5{y}_{2}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what is missing from the blank spaces?"] [#edb/ref 17592186357671 "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)=3{x}_{1}^{2}+5{x}_{2}^{2}-6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n3{y}_{1}^{2}+\\boxed{}\\,{y}_{2}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what is missing from the blank spaces?"] [#edb/ref 17592186357672 "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}+38{x}_{2}^{2}+16{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n\\boxed{}\\,{y}_{1}^{2}+6{y}_{2}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2}={x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what is missing from the blank spaces?"] [#edb/ref 17592186357676 "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+26{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2}-10{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-10{x}_{2}{x}_{3}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}+2{y}_{3}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{3}={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom, what is missing from the blank spaces?"] [#edb/ref 17592186357677 "Lagrange's method can be used to reduce the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}$ to the canonical form given below. \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}-2{y}_{3}^{2},\\,{\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{2}=\\boxed{} \\\\ {y}_{3}={x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom top to bottom, what is missing from the blank spaces?"] [#edb/ref 17592186360768 "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}y+2z-x=1 \\\\ 6y+3x-2z=2 \\\\ x+3z-y=-3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}a & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & b & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186362398 "Find the limit at $x=-1$ of the piecewise function $f(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt[3]{x}\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x<-1 \\\\ -2\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x=-1 \\\\ x+2\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x>-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186362399 "For the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-x\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x\\le -1 \\\\ x+c\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x>-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nit is known that ${lim}_{x\\to -1}f(x)=1.$ What is the value of the constant $c?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186362400 "Find ${lim}_{x\\to (-2)^{-}}f(x)$ and ${lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}f(x)$ for the function given by\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}-x & \\text{ for }\\,x<-2 \\\\ x & \\text{ for }\\,x>3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186362401 "Find ${lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}f(x)$ and ${lim}_{x\\to {1}^{+}}f(x)$ for the function given by\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & \\text{ for }\\,x<-1 \\\\ 3 & \\text{ for }\\,x>1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186363087 "Consider the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}-15{x}_{3}=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form."] [#edb/ref 17592186363094 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-3x-3y+6z=9 \\\\ -x+4z=4 \\\\ x+y-2z=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system."] [#edb/ref 17592186363101 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y=-1 \\\\ 2x-5y-3z=6 \\\\ -x+2y=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system."] [#edb/ref 17592186363108 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-3y+z=2 \\\\  & -2x+7y+2z=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system has no solution\n- **III.** The system is consistent independent"] [#edb/ref 17592186363217 "$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & {a}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | \\\\ {q}_{1} & {q}_{2} & {q}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}{r}_{11} & {r}_{12} & {r}_{13} \\\\ 0 & {r}_{22} & {r}_{23} \\\\ 0 & 0 & {r}_{33}\\end{bmatrix}}}\n$$\n\nConsider the QR factorization of the matrix $A$ shown above. You're given that the system of equations given below connects the columns of $Q$ and the columns of $A.$  \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1}=\\frac{1}{4}{a}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{2}+{q}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{3}=\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{3}+2{q}_{1}-{q}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of ${r}_{13}+{r}_{22}+{r}_{23}?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186363405 "![](images/8f/8f955ee719a4e69f0d09c678f0a74023f137efd7b5ae36d49b98706156384173.png)\n\nConsider the function $f(x)$ whose graph is shown above.\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}x+\\frac{1}{2},\\, & 0<x<1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x$\n- ${\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked."] [#edb/ref 17592186363479 "Suppose we would like to find the minimum value of the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}-y+z$ on the intersection of the surfaces ${y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1$ and ${x}^{2}+z=4$ using the method of Lagrange multipliers. Then, the corresponding Lagrange multipliers $\\lambda $ and $\\mu $ satisfy the following system: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}⟨2x,\\,-1,\\,1⟩=\\lambda ⟨0,\\,,\\,2z⟩+\\mu ⟨2x,\\,,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+z=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing expressions?"] [#edb/ref 17592186363486 "Suppose we would like to find the maximum value of the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}-yz$ on the intersection of the surfaces $y+{z}^{2}=1$ and ${x}^{2}+z=4$ using the method of Lagrange multipliers. Then, the corresponding Lagrange multipliers $\\lambda $ and $\\mu $ satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}⟨2x,\\,-z,\\,-y⟩=\\lambda ⟨0,\\,1,\\,\\,⟩+\\mu ⟨2x,\\,0,\\,\\,⟩ \\\\ y+{z}^{2}=1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+z=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing expressions?"] [#edb/ref 17592186363493 "Suppose we would like to find the maximum of the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}y+{z}^{2}$ on the intersection of the surfaces $y-{x}^{2}=1$ and ${x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=4$ using the method of Lagrange multipliers. Then, the corresponding Lagrange multipliers $\\lambda $ and $\\mu $ satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}⟨\\,,\\,{x}^{2},\\,2z⟩=\\lambda ⟨\\,,\\,1,\\,0⟩+\\mu ⟨2x,\\,,\\,2z⟩ \\\\ y-{x}^{2}=1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the expressions?"] [#edb/ref 17592186363988 "If the following system of differential equations is written in the form ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ then what is the matrix $A?$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)-2{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)+8{x}_{1}(t)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186364027 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)-6{x}_{1}(t)+7{x}_{2}(t)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)+t\\,{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system of linear ODEs above can be written in matrix form as follows:\n\n| ${x}^{′}(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,x(t)+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-3}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-4}} | {{field-5}} |  |  | {{field-6}} |  |  |  |  |"] [#edb/ref 17592186364047 "Which of the following systems are homogeneous?\n- **I.** ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}$\n- **II.** ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+5\\end{aligned}$\n- **III.** ${\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=7{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked."] [#edb/ref 17592186364171 "$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & {a}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | \\\\ \\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖} & \\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖} & \\frac{{v}_{3}}{‖{v}_{3}‖} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}{r}_{11} & {r}_{12} & {r}_{13} \\\\ 0 & {r}_{22} & {r}_{23} \\\\ 0 & 0 & {r}_{33}\\end{bmatrix}}}\n$$\n\nConsider the QR factorization of the matrix $A$ shown above, where ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is an orthogonal set of vectors. You're given that $‖{v}_{1}‖=3,$ $‖{v}_{2}‖=4,$ $‖{v}_{3}‖=2,$ and that the system of equations below describes the relationship between the columns of $Q$ and the columns of $A.$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}={a}_{1} \\\\ {v}_{2}={a}_{2}-3{v}_{1} \\\\ {v}_{3}={a}_{3}-5{v}_{1}-2{v}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of ${r}_{13}+{r}_{22}+{r}_{33}?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186364178 "$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & {a}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | \\\\ {q}_{1} & {q}_{2} & {q}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}{r}_{11} & {r}_{12} & {r}_{13} \\\\ 0 & {r}_{22} & {r}_{23} \\\\ 0 & 0 & {r}_{33}\\end{bmatrix}}}\n$$\n\nConsider the QR factorization of the matrix $A$ shown above. You're given that the system of equations given below connects the columns of $Q$ and the columns of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1}=\\frac{1}{6}{a}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{2}+8{q}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{3}=\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{3}-3{q}_{1}+2{q}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of ${r}_{13}+{r}_{22}+{r}_{33}?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186364358 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-y+2z=0 \\\\  & 3x-2y+6z=-1 \\\\  & -2x+2y-z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form."] [#edb/ref 17592186364365 "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 3x+2y=8 \\\\  & x+y=-2 \\\\  & x+\\frac{1}{2}y=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system has no solution\n- **II.** The system is consistent independent\n- **III.** The system is consistent dependent"] [#edb/ref 17592186364599 "$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & {a}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | \\\\ \\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖} & \\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖} & \\frac{{v}_{3}}{‖{v}_{3}‖} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}{r}_{11} & {r}_{12} & {r}_{13} \\\\ 0 & {r}_{22} & {r}_{23} \\\\ 0 & 0 & {r}_{33}\\end{bmatrix}}}\n$$\n\nConsider the QR factorization of the matrix $A$ shown above, where ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is an orthogonal set of vectors. You're given that $‖{v}_{1}‖=1,$ $‖{v}_{2}‖=3,$ $‖{v}_{3}‖=2,$ and that the system of equations below describes the relationship between the columns of $Q$ and the columns of $A.$ \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}={a}_{1} \\\\ {v}_{2}={a}_{2}-3{v}_{1} \\\\ {v}_{3}={a}_{3}-{v}_{1}-2{v}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of ${r}_{12}+{r}_{22}+{r}_{23}?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186364606 "$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & {a}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | \\\\ \\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖} & \\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖} & \\frac{{v}_{3}}{‖{v}_{3}‖} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}{r}_{11} & {r}_{12} & {r}_{13} \\\\ 0 & {r}_{22} & {r}_{23} \\\\ 0 & 0 & {r}_{33}\\end{bmatrix}}}\n$$\n\nConsider the QR factorization of the matrix $A$ shown above, where ${{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}}$ is an orthogonal set of vectors. You're given that $‖{v}_{1}‖=6,$ $‖{v}_{2}‖=3,$ $‖{v}_{3}‖=2,$ and that the system of equations below describes the relationship between the columns of $Q$ and the columns of $A.$ \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}={a}_{1} \\\\ {v}_{2}={a}_{2}+{v}_{1} \\\\ {v}_{3}={a}_{3}-2{v}_{1}+{v}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of ${r}_{22}+{r}_{23}+{r}_{33}?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186364763 "The second-order initial value problem\n\n$$\n12{y}^{″}+5{y}^{′}-2y=0,\\,y(1)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=-2\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{1}(1)=p \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}=f(t),\\, & {x}_{2}(1)=q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{′}(t),$ and $p$ and $q$ are constants. Calculate  $(p-q)\\cdot f(t).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186364777 "The third-order differential equation ${y}^{‴}+6t{y}^{″}+8{t}^{2}y=0$\ncan be expressed as the matrix equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where \n\n$$\nx(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & a \\\\ 0 & 0 & b \\\\ -8{t}^{2} & 0 & c\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nand for $y=y(t),$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y={x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}={x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {y}^{″}={x}_{3}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the value of $a+b+c.$"] [#e