c{1}{7}, & x\\ge 7,\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186399622 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=6+2t \\\\ y=5+t \\\\ z=-3-3t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:5x+3y-4z=-43.\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186399629 "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=4+2t \\\\ y=-3+4t \\\\ z=5t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:3x+2y-z=33.\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186399678 "The second-order initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-4{e}^{t}{y}^{′}+5y=0,\\,y(0)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-1\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{1}(0)=p \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}=f(t),\\, & {x}_{2}(0)=q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{′}(t),$ and $p$ and $q$ are constants. Calculate  $(p-q)\\cdot f(t).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186400282 "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=4t \\\\ y=-2t \\\\ z=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat would be the vector equation of the line?"] [#edb/ref 17592186400289 "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=5-9t \\\\ y=-2+7t \\\\ z=-8t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat would be the vector equation of the line?"] [#edb/ref 17592186400296 "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=13-8t \\\\ y=7t \\\\ z=-7-3t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat would be the vector equation of the line?"] [#edb/ref 17592186400513 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y-z=4 \\\\  & -3x-6y+4z=-8 \\\\  & 3x+7y-z=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system."] [#edb/ref 17592186400618 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{