) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=4{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=2.$*"] [#edb/ref 17592186402113 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=2y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the general solution to the system of ODEs above?\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{2t} & t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$*"] [#edb/ref 17592186402154 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=x(t)+2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=3x(t)-y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives all equilibrium points of the system of linear differential equations above?"] [#edb/ref 17592186402161 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=x(t)+3y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=2x(t)+5y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives all equilibrium points of the system of linear differential equations above?"] [#edb/ref 17592186402168 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}=2x(1-2x)-xy \\\\ {y}^{′}=-y+xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the Lotka-Volterra model with carrying capacity above, where $x=x(t)$ represents the prey and $y=y(t)$ represents the predators. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.$\\,$ Evaluating the Jacobian of the system at the equilibrium ${x}^{∗}=[0,\\,0]^{T},$ we get\n\n$$J(x^{\\ast})=\\begin{bmatrix}{{field-1}}&{{field-2}}\\\\{{field-3}}&{{field-4}}\\end{bmatrix}.$$\n\n$\\,$ The eigenvalues of the Jacobian matrix are \n{{field-5}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the equilibrium at ${x}^{∗}$ is \n{{field-6}}{{field-7}}."] [#edb/ref 17592186402302 "$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-1, & x\\in [-4,0] \\\\ 3, & x\\in (0,4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the function $F(x)$ shown above. The Fourier series of the $8$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼1+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{8}{\\pi (2n-1)}sin\\,(\\frac{(2n-1)\\pi x}{4}).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nAt $x=-2,$