 above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation, we get the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{{field-1}}={{field-2}} \\\\ {{field-3}}=-5{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively."] [#edb/ref 17592186434054 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{2}(t)+5,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=$ {{field-1}} $,\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{s+5}{s(s-2)}.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186434055 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)+5,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=-\\frac{3}{s+2},\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-1}}."] [#edb/ref 17592186434056 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)+{t}^{2}-4 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)+5,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation, we get the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)+1={{field-1}}-\\frac{4}{s} \\\\ {{field-2}}={X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)+{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively."] [#edb/ref 17592186434057 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)+2{e}^{-t} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)+3,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation, we get the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{{field-1}}=2{X}_{1}(s)+{{field-2}} \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)+1={X}_{1}(s)+{X}_{2}(s)+{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}$ are the Laplace transforms of the functions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t),$ respectively."] [#edb/ref 17592186434058 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)+4 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{2}(t)-1,\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{1}{s-1}+\\frac{1}{s-3}-\\frac{1}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{2}{s-1}+\\frac{1}{s}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>"] [#edb/ref 17592186434059 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the 