h variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=-\\frac{s+2}{s(s-3)},\\,$\n${X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-1}}."] [#edb/ref 17592186434097 "Given that the random variable $X∼{χ}^{2}(8),$ calculate $P(X<6).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places.\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following result:*\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{6}{x}^{3}{e}^{-x/2}\\,\\text{d}x≈33.86574\n$$\n\n*The probability density function ${χ}^{2}(k)$ is given by*\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{2}^{k/2}Γ(\\frac{k}{2})}{x}^{k/2-1}{e}^{-x/2}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186434098 "Given that $X∼{χ}^{2}(8),$ what is $P(X<6)$ expressed as an integral?\n\n*Hint: The probability density function ${χ}^{2}(k)$ is given by*\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{2}^{k/2}Γ(\\frac{k}{2})}{x}^{k/2-1}{e}^{-x/2}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186434425 "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x, & 0<x<1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\,x, & 1\\le x<2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$"] [#edb/ref 17592186434814 "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]≈1.238\\,10,$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}, & 0<x<1 \\\\ \\frac{2{x}^{2}}{7}, & 1\\le x<2, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186434815 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{8},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186434816 "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given th