 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x+y}, & x\\le 0,\\,y\\le 0, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe marginal CDF ${F}_{Y}(y)$ of $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{F}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}g(y), & y\\le 0 \\\\ 1 & y>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat is the function $g(y)?$"] [#edb/ref 17592186476893 "Find $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}{Y}^{2}],$ given that random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}y+1,\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,-1\\le y\\le 0, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186476905 "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P((X-1)^{2}+{Y}^{2}<1).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186476909 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y), & 0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(-\\frac{\\pi }{6}<Y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{12}).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186476911 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x{y}^{2}}{4}, & \\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the marginal PDF ${f}_{Y}(y).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186476913 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y), & 0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the marginal PDF ${f}_{Y}(y).$"] [#edb/ref 1759