omain of $f.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186496252 "Given the system of equations below, what is the value of $y-x?$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}21x-9y=0 \\\\ 5y-15x+10=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186496255 "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+y=-4 \\\\ x-3y=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(x,y)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$(x,y)=($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$"] [#edb/ref 17592186496256 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-2y=22 \\\\ 5x+8y=14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe variable $y$ can be eliminated from the system using the following two steps:\n\n1\\. Multiply the first equation by $4$ and obtain\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}12x-8y=88.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\n2\\. Add the multiplied equation to the second equation to get\n\n$\\,$\n{{field-1}}$=102.$\n\n$\\,$\nHence, the solution to the system of equations is $($\n{{field-2}}$\\,,$\n{{field-3}}\n$).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186496258 "Let $X$ be a random variable with the probability density function shown below. What is the mode of $X?$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}{e}^{-2x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186496264 "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the ellipsoid $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}+3{z}^{2}=1$ and the line \n$\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-t \\\\ y=t, \\\\ z=t\\end{aligned}$ where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186496269 "Let $X$ be a random variable with the probability density function shown below. What is the mode of $X?$\n\n$f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{24}x,\\, & 1\\le x\\le 7 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}$"] [#edb/ref 17592186496287 "Using the elimination method, eliminate the variable $a$ and find the solution $(a,b)$ to the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2a+3b=-5 \\\\ -2a+3b=11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}$\\,,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186496289 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}4r+9v=3 \\\\ 8r-2v=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe variable $r$ can be eliminated from the system using the following two steps:\n\n1\\. Multiply the first equation by $-2$ and obtain\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}-8r-18v & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\n2\\. Add the multiplied equation to the second equation to get\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}⋯\\,\\,?\\,\\,⋯\\,\\,=-5.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\nWhat's the missing expression?"] [#edb/ref 17592186496304 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}4u+5p=24 \\\\ 5u+p=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe variable $p$ can be eliminated from the system using the following two steps:\n\n1\\. Multiply the second equation by $-5$ and obtain\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}-25u-5p=-45.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\n2\\. Add the multiplied equation to the first equation to get\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}⋯\\,\\,?\\,\\,⋯\\,\\,=-21.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\nFind the missing expression, and hence find the solution $(u,p)$ of the system."] [#edb/ref 17592186496305 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x+7y=-20 \\\\ 4x-y=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe variable $y$ can be eliminated from the system using the following two steps:\n\n1\\. Multiply the second equation by $7$ and obtain\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}28x-7y=-49.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\n2\\. Add the multiplied equation to the first equation to get\n\n$\\,$\n{{field-1}}$=-69.$\n\n$\\,$\nHence, the solution to the system of equations is $($\n{{field-2}}$\\,,$\n{{field-3}}\n$).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186496314 "Consider the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3p-6q=-18 \\\\ 4p+3q+2=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(p,q)$ to this system using the method of substitution.\n\n$(p,q)=($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$"] [#edb/ref 17592186496321 "Find the solution $(u,t)$ to the following system of equations using the elimination method:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-u+2t=-2 \\\\ 3u-2t=10\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [#edb/ref 17592186496322 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+y=6 \\\\ 3x+4y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe variable $y$ can be eliminated from the system using the following two steps:\n\n1\\. Multiply the first equation by $-4$ and obtain\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}8x-4y=-24.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\n2\\. Add the multiplied equation to the second equation to get\n\n$\\,$\n{{field-1}}$=-22.$\n\n$\\,$\nHence, the solution to the system of equations is $($\n{{field-2}}$\\,,$\n{{field-3}}\n$).$"] [#edb/ref 17592186496330 "Consider the following system of equations. \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-5y=-12 \\\\ x+3y=20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe variable $x$ can be eliminated from the system using the following two steps:\n\n1\\. Multiply the first equation by $-1$ and obtain\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}-x+5y & =12.\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\n2\\. Add the multiplied equation to the second equation to get\n\n$\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$=32.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186497359 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}=4x(1-0.25x)-3xy \\\\ {y}^{′}=-y+xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the Lotka-Volterra model with carrying capacity above, where $x=x(t)$ represents the prey and $y=y(t)$ represents the predators. The equilibria of the model are the following:\n\n$(0,0),\\,(${{field-1}}$,0),\\,(${{field-2}}$,${{field-3}}$)$"] [#edb/ref 17592186497388 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}=2x(1-x)-2xy \\\\ {y}^{′}=-2y+3xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the Lotka-Volterra model with carrying capacity above, where $x=x(t)$ represents the prey and $y=y(t)$ represents the predators. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\n$\\,$ Evaluating the Jacobian of the system at the equilibrium ${x}^{∗}=[0,\\,0]^{T},$ we get\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$J({x}^{∗})=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<