.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186520464 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6{x}^{2}+6y}{5}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0<y<1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6y+2}{5}, & 0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the expression for the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]$ for $0<y<1.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186520466 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2(x+2y)}{3}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1+4y}{3}, & 0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the expression for the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]$ for $0\\le y\\le 1.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186520474 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3x{y}^{2}}{4}, & 0\\le y\\le 2,\\,0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}2x, & 0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the expression for the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=x]$ for $0<x<1.$"] [#edb/ref 17592186520489 "$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,3)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{8}, & \\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=3]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,3)$ is shown above."] [#edb/ref 17592186520491 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+3y}{12}, & 1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y+1}{4}, & 0\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=1].$"] [#edb/ref 17592186520492 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}8xy, & 0<x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le x, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{3}, & 0<x\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1].$"] [#edb/ref 17592186520503 "$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,1)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1+{y}^{2}}{12}, & \\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)$ is shown above."] [#edb/ref 17592186521554 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}=3x(1-0.5x)-2xy \\\\ {y}^{′}=-4y+4xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the Lotka-Volterra model with carrying capacity above, where $x=x(t)$ represents the prey and $y=y(t)$ represents the predators. The equilibria of the model are the following:\n\n$(0,0),\\,(${{field-1}}$,0),\\,(${{field-2}}$,${{field-3}}$)$"] [#edb/ref 17592186521560 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}=2x(1-0.05x)-3xy \\\\ {y}^{′}=-4y+2xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the Lotka-Volterra model with carrying capacity above, where $x=x(t)$ represents the prey and $y=y(t)$ represents the predators. The equilibria of the model are the following:\n\n$(0,0),\\,(${{field-1}}$,0),\\,(${{field-2}}$,${{field-3}}$)$"] [#edb/ref 17592186523101 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=0 \\\\ x+4y=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system is consistent independent\n- **III.** The system is inconsistent"] [#edb/ref 17592186523112 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-2z=-4 \\\\ x+3y=-8 \\\\ x+y-4z=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent independent\n- **II.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **III.** The system is inconsistent"] [#edb/ref 17592186523119 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y=-5 \\\\ -2x+6y=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system is consistent independent\n- **III.** The system is inconsistent"] [#edb/ref 17592186523120 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+2z=0 \\\\ -2x-y-7z=-2 \\\\ 2x+11z=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent independent\n- **II.** The system is inconsistent\n- **III.** The system is consistent dependent"] [#edb/ref 17592186523134 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+z=5 \\\\ x+2y+2z=7 \\\\ x+3y+5z=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system is consistent independent\n- **III.** The system is inconsistent"] [#edb/ref 17592186523146 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-z=1 \\\\ 2x+5y=7 \\\\ -2x-3y+5z=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is inconsistent\n- **II.** The system is consistent independent\n- **III.** The system is consistent dependent"] [#edb/ref 17592186523149 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y=1 \\\\ 2x+4y=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system is inconsistent\n- **III.** The system is consistent independent"] [#edb/ref 17592186523165 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y=4 \\\\ -x=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system is consistent independent\n- **III.** The system is inconsistent"] [#edb/ref 17592186523181 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y-3z=5 \\\\ 2x-5y-9z=10 \\\\ 2x-5y-9z=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system is inconsistent\n- **III.** The system is consistent independent"] [#edb/ref 17592186523190 "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=-3 \\\\ -2x-4y=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent independent\n- **II.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **III.** The system is inconsistent"] [#edb/ref 17592186523934 "![](images/48/483c019e9c68f857379192d2b40ab84803c4360ca4e0158adc0a8a3bc1636c4e.png)\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables with the joint probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+\\frac{8}{9}xy, & (x,y)\\in D, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.